From 2943c74651d562fea0bdcb7948a1b8917767215a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A2Tools-patch <patch@localhost>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:44:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/33] Odyle energy: never another character's shown as live

After switching to a twink the meter's title showed the last character's
Odyle energy (390 (+50)) as live while the game said 0. The window kept the
last value it was sent: when the backend no longer knew the energy (a
login's list that didn't read), it sent nothing. Now it tells the window
(`cleared`), and the window shows energy named for another character than
the one playing only as that character's, never as the current one's.

A character with no energy has the entry with no value (`00`, both 0). In
a list that doesn't read whole, the energy found by its id was only taken
in the forms with a value: now `00` too. A login's list that doesn't read
is logged with its size.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RahWACwaxzLAcYgwc9jk8C
